<GuideArticle slug="can-you-walk-to-a-beach-from-downtown-oranjestad"
  title="Can you walk to a beach from downtown Oranjestad?"
  metaTitle="Can You Walk to a Beach from Downtown Oranjestad, Aruba? Honest Distances"
  description="Yes — Surfside Beach is a 15-minute flat walk from downtown Oranjestad, and Eagle Beach is a 10-minute drive. The honest guide to staying in the city and still getting your beach days."
  kicker="Beaches · the honest answer" faq={faq}>
  <p>We'll answer this the way we'd want it answered, because it's the main question about staying downtown — and because we'd rather you knew before booking than after. <strong>Yes, you can walk to a beach from downtown Oranjestad — and no, downtown is not a beachfront location.</strong> Both halves are true.</p>
  <h2>The walkable one: Surfside Beach</h2>
  <p><strong>Surfside Beach is about 1.2 km from central Oranjestad — a 15-minute flat walk</strong> south along the Linear Park waterfront path, past the harbour and the airport fence. It's a calm, sheltered, genuinely swimmable beach with soft sand, a beach bar or two, and a front-row view of landing aircraft that kids tend to love. It is a local's beach, not a postcard — smaller and simpler than the famous strips.</p>
  <h2>The famous one: Eagle Beach</h2>
  <p><strong>Eagle Beach — regularly ranked among the best beaches in the Caribbean — is about 4.5 km away: a 10-minute drive, a short bus ride, or a ~$10 taxi.</strong> Wide, white, uncrowded by Caribbean standards, with the famous fofoti trees. If your Aruba picture is that picture, it's ten minutes from your door, not at it.</p>
  <h2>So who should stay downtown?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stay downtown if</strong> you want to walk to dinner every night (dining is the island's biggest discretionary spend for a reason), see the harbour from a pool deck, and treat beaches as outings.</li>
    <li><strong>Stay at Palm or Eagle Beach if</strong> you want to step from your room onto sand and will mostly eat at your resort.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We say this on our own homepage: the guests who want a resort strip should book a resort strip. The guests who want the city — with Surfside on foot and Eagle ten minutes away — are the ones who leave the five-star reviews here.</p>
  <h2>A beach-day pattern that works from Oranjestad</h2>
  <p>Morning swim at Surfside on foot before the heat; one full Eagle Beach day mid-trip with a taxi both ways; sunset back in town on the waterfront with dinner a block away. Three beach experiences, zero car rental.</p>
</GuideArticle>
